Input: {"question": "Which sports team does Mamadou N'Diaye represent or represent?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 65, "text": "Title: The Unlikely Giant: Mamadou N'Diaye's Journey to UC Irvine"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 67, "end": 219, "text": "In the heart of Dakar, Senegal, a young Mamadou N'Diaye was born in 1993, with a passion for basketball that would take him on an extraordinary journey."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 220, "end": 434, "text": "Little did he know that his towering height and natural talent would one day lead him to the sun-kissed courts of California, where he would become an integral part of the UC Irvine Anteaters men's basketball team."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 435, "end": 527, "text": "Growing up in Senegal, Mamadou's love for basketball was nurtured by his family and friends."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 528, "end": 639, "text": "He would spend hours playing pickup games in the streets, honing his skills and developing a strong work ethic."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 640, "end": 779, "text": "As he grew taller, his dominance on the court became apparent, and it wasn't long before college scouts from the United States took notice."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 780, "end": 896, "text": "In 2013, Mamadou made the bold decision to leave his homeland and pursue his basketball dreams in the United States."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 897, "end": 1045, "text": "He enrolled at Stoneridge Prep in Simi Valley, California, where he would spend a year refining his game and adapting to the American style of play."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1046, "end": 1177, "text": "It was during this time that he caught the attention of college coaches, including those from the University of California, Irvine."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1178, "end": 1281, "text": "UC Irvine, a mid-major program with a growing reputation, saw immense potential in the 7-foot-6 center."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1282, "end": 1389, "text": "They offered him a scholarship, and Mamadou accepted, becoming the tallest player in the program's history."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1390, "end": 1548, "text": "As he donned the Anteaters' uniform, he brought with him a unique set of skills, including his imposing presence in the paint and a soft touch around the rim."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1549, "end": 1580, "text": "Mamadou's impact was immediate."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1581, "end": 1727, "text": "In his freshman year, he averaged 10.5 points, 7.1 rebounds, and 2.4 blocks per game, earning him Big West Conference Freshman of the Year honors."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1728, "end": 1878, "text": "His dominance continued throughout his collegiate career, as he led the Anteaters to multiple postseason appearances and set numerous program records."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1879, "end": 2010, "text": "One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Mamadou's affiliation with UC Irvine is his impressive statistical record."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2011, "end": 2141, "text": "According to the NCAA, Mamadou played in 127 games for the Anteaters, averaging 9.4 points, 6.4 rebounds, and 2.1 blocks per game."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "Mamadou N'Diaye"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 17, "end": 198, "text": "Mamadou N'Diaye (born 1993) is a Senegalese professional basketball player who currently plays for Colchester United F.C., an association football club based in Colchester, England."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 199, "end": 220, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 222, "end": 277, "text": "N'Diaye was born on August 12, 1993, in Dakar, Senegal."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 278, "end": 421, "text": "He began playing basketball at a young age and quickly rose through the ranks, earning a spot on the Senegalese national team by the age of 18."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 422, "end": 597, "text": "In 2012, he moved to Europe to pursue a professional career, playing for several clubs in Spain and France before making the unexpected switch to association football in 2018."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 598, "end": 632, "text": "Transfer to Colchester United F.C."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 633, "end": 771, "text": "On August 15, 2018, N'Diaye signed a two-year contract with Colchester United F.C., becoming the first Senegalese player to join the club."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 772, "end": 854, "text": "The move was seen as a surprise by many, given N'Diaye's background in basketball."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 855, "end": 1008, "text": "However, the club's manager, John McGreal, expressed confidence in N'Diaye's ability to adapt to the sport, citing his athleticism and strong work ethic."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1009, "end": 1031, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1033, "end": 1267, "text": "A study published in the Journal of Sports Science and Medicine in 2019 found that basketball players who transition to association football tend to exhibit improved agility and speed compared to players who have only played football."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1268, "end": 1488, "text": "The study, which analyzed data from 20 professional players, including N'Diaye, concluded that the crossover between the two sports can be beneficial for athletes looking to improve their overall fitness and performance."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1489, "end": 1492, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1494, "end": 1716, "text": "In an interview with The Guardian in 2020, N'Diaye discussed his decision to switch sports, stating, \"I've always been passionate about football, and I saw this as an opportunity to challenge myself and learn a new skill.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1717, "end": 1894, "text": "He also praised the support of his teammates and coaches at Colchester United, saying, \"They've been amazing, helping me to adjust to the new game and pushing me to be my best.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1895, "end": 1898, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1900, "end": 2108, "text": "A report by the BBC in 2020 highlighted N'Diaye's impressive debut season with Colchester United, during which he scored 5 goals in 20 appearances and helped the team secure a spot in the League Two playoffs."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2109, "end": 2232, "text": "The report noted that N'Diaye's basketball background had given him an edge in terms of his speed and agility on the pitch."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "UC Irvine Anteaters", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Colchester United F.C.", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "Senegalese national basketball team", "card_ids": ["d2:c1"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Mamadou N'Diaye", "scope": "sports team", "claim": "Mamadou N'Diaye represents the UC Irvine Anteaters men's basketball team.", "answer": "UC Irvine Anteaters", "quote": "Little did he know that his towering height and natural talent would one day lead him to the sun-kissed courts of California, where he would become an integral part of the UC Irvine Anteaters men's basketball team. Growing up in Senegal, Mamadou's love for basketball was nurtured by his family and friends. He would spend hours playing pickup games in the streets, honing his skills and developing a strong work ethic. As he grew taller, his dominance on the court became apparent, and it wasn't long before college scouts from the United States took notice. In 2013, Mamadou made the bold decision to leave his homeland and pursue his basketball dreams in the United States. He enrolled at Stoneridge Prep in Simi Valley, California, where he would spend a year refining his game and adapting to the American style of play. It was during this time that he caught the attention of college coaches, including those from the University of California, Irvine. UC Irvine, a mid-major program with a growing reputation, saw immense potential in the 7-foot-6 center. They offered him a scholarship, and Mamadou accepted, becoming the tallest player in the program's history. As he donned the Anteaters' uniform, he brought with him a unique set of skills, including his imposing presence in the paint and a soft touch around the rim.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Mamadou N'Diaye", "scope": "current", "claim": "Mamadou N'Diaye currently represents Colchester United F.C.", "answer": "Colchester United F.C.", "quote": "Mamadou N'Diaye (born 1993) is a Senegalese professional basketball player who currently plays for Colchester United F.C., an association football club based in Colchester, England.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "Mamadou N'Diaye", "scope": "past", "claim": "Mamadou N'Diaye represented the Senegalese national basketball team before the age of 18.", "answer": "Senegalese national basketball team", "quote": "He began playing basketball at a young age and quickly rose through the ranks, earning a spot on the Senegalese national team by the age of 18.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["UC Irvine Anteaters", "Colchester United F.C.", "Senegalese national basketball team"]}
